# Curated SuiteSparse Matrix Collection corpus for DirectLUSolvers.
#
# Download with:  python fetch_suitesparse.py
# Consumed by:    test/test_suitesparse.cpp  (via testing/TestData.h)
#
# The files themselves live in cache/ and are NOT committed. This manifest is,
# so the corpus is reproducible: SuiteSparse matrices are immutable, so a given
# line always denotes the same matrix.
#
# WHY THESE MATRICES
#
# The selection is stratified on PATTERN SYMMETRY (psym), because that is the
# axis these solvers are actually sensitive to. Both factor a symmetric pattern,
# so a matrix whose pattern is far from symmetric gets explicit structural zeros
# added and can fill catastrophically -- a corpus of psym==1.00 matrices would
# look great and test nothing about the failure mode that matters. The bands:
#
#   psym == 1.00   native symmetric pattern -- the intended use case
#   0.50 - 0.99    partial -- symmetrization adds moderate structure
#   < 0.50         strongly unsymmetric -- stress case; several of these are
#                  EXPECTED to be declined by the fill guard, and that is a
#                  tested behaviour, not a failure
#
# Within each band the pick spreads over problem kind (structural, CFD, circuit,
# chemical process, thermal, graph, ...) and size, taking a mid-sized
# representative of each family rather than the extremes.
#
# TIERS
#   quick     small, runs in CI
#   standard  larger; run on demand
#   large     big enough to need real time/memory
#
# Add candidates with:  python fetch_suitesparse.py --propose 20
# Check the metadata is still accurate:  python fetch_suitesparse.py --verify
#
# group name tier n nnz psym spd kind

# --- band: native symmetric pattern (psym == 1.00) -------------------------
